# 0002 (Strata v0.2.11 / main at 9f7d977; src/split/src/model.cpp + docs/SPLIT_ENGINE.md): FNX_POOL_MIN_RESIDENT.
# An optional per-pool floor in choose_residency(): the coldest-by-bytes eviction never takes a size pool below N resident experts
# (default 0 = upstream behaviour). Needed for mixed-quant files such as IQ3_S. This is upstream PR #5258.
# Apply with: git apply patches/0002-pool-min-resident.patch
# On v0.2.10 the model.cpp hunk applies as is; skip the docs hunk: git apply --exclude=docs/SPLIT_ENGINE.md patches/0002-pool-min-resident.patch

# split: add FNX_POOL_MIN_RESIDENT, an optional per-pool floor in choose_residency() (default off = unchanged)
#
# The expert cache needs 2*MAXT*TOPK (320) slots in every size pool, but
# choose_residency() moves the coldest-per-byte experts to host memory first,
# which empties the small pools of mixed-quant files (IQ3_S: pool 3 is only
# 3 layers) and place_experts() then throws "pool P has K slots, a window
# needs 320". On 16 GB cards no value of FNX_EXPERT_RAM_GIB worked.
#
# FNX_POOL_MIN_RESIDENT=N never takes a size pool below N resident experts.
# The "VRAM short" loop goes through the same function, so the floor applies
# there too. Unset or 0 keeps the upstream behaviour. Documented in
# docs/SPLIT_ENGINE.md.
#
# Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
#

